{"skill":{"slug":"google-search","displayName":"google-search"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769909754813,"changelog":"- Initial release of the Google Search skill for OpenClaw agents.\n- Enables web searches via Google's Custom Search API (PSE).\n- Provides setup instructions for API key and Programmable Search Engine ID.\n- Includes usage example for performing searches from the command line.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":946,"sha256":"d9600f3dc7af3761e2b2f421e05e78238f1f11d2e22cad0a35160bb1697c11a2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/search.py","size":1099,"sha256":"bebf186b146545beac53401f102c82188dd5a3c9c9bf1a77d31fe672ac53a26b","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1777,"sha256":"9471eaa7acd3090252ef298553b6fccdd93897e6c3f2eee1afdfea0aaecc93e1","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789025726151,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"e2dfe0b481754d2777da11ba9133a5f951474b37b6e89f3227a839868ec6dfe4","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/e2dfe0b481754d2777da11ba9133a5f951474b37b6e89f3227a839868ec6dfe4","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: google-search\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThis skill bundle is classified as benign. The `scripts/search.py` script correctly implements a Google Custom Search functionality, securely retrieving API keys (`GOOGLE_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_CSE_ID`) from environment variables using `os.getenv`. It only makes network requests to the official Google Custom Search API endpoint (`https://www.googleapis.com/customsearch/v1`). The `SKILL.md` documentation provides clear setup instructions and does not contain any prompt injection attempts or instructions for the agent to perform malicious actions.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160583829},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":9,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789025726151},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This Google search skill is purpose-aligned, but its error handling can expose the user's Google API key and search details in logs or agent output.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Using GOOGLE_API_KEY and GOOGLE_CSE_ID is proportionate for Google Custom Search, but the script prints raw exception strings from failed requests, which can include the full request URL containing the key, search engine ID, and query.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact contains a SKILL.md and one local Python script; no installer, dependency bootstrapper, remote payload retrieval, or self-modifying setup behavior was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions disclose the need for Google API credentials and outbound Google API access, but they provide only minimal workflow detail and no explicit permission or endpoint scope declaration.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, background service, scheduled task, memory writing, privilege escalation, or tool hijacking behavior was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill's stated purpose is web search through Google Custom Search, and the bundled script only performs a Google Custom Search API request and prints the JSON response.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use a restricted Google API key, avoid sensitive searches, and be aware that failed API calls may print credential-bearing request details until the script sanitizes errors and adds safer exception handling.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Outbound network access and environment variables are expected for a Google Custom Search helper, but the artifact does not declare a narrow permission or endpoint scope, so this remains a governance and disclosure note rather than evidence of malicious behavior.\n[T09] unexpected: The scanner concern is supported by artifact evidence: scripts/search.py passes the API key, search engine ID, and query as request parameters and then prints str(e) for any exception, which can disclose sensitive request data on API errors.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789025726151}}}}}